TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> Investigators were reviewing a range of possible terror links to a gunman who opened fire at a crowded Orlando nightclub early Sunday, leaving at least 50 dead and 53 others wounded. A federal law enforcement official identified the attacker as Omar Mateen of Port St. Lucie, Fla. The official, who is not authorized to comment publicly, said Mateen is a U.S. citizen, and investigators were reviewing whether Mate
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> President-elect Donald Trump has chosen Wilbur Ross Jr., a billionaire investor and turnaround specialist, as his commerce secretary.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> In Alexandria, an explosion outside St Mark's Coptic church killed 13 people. Pope Tawadros II, head of the Coptic Church, had been attending Mass inside and was unhurt, state media reported.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> After months of uncertainty, President Trump will announce on Tuesday that he is ending a controversial program that protects nearly 800,000 young undocumented immigrants from deportation, media reports indicated late Sunday.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> The House passed a bill Tuesday that would ban abortions after 20 weeks.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> President Trump explicitly endorsed embattled candidate Roy Moore on Monday, saying he needs a Republican in the Alabama seat to help push through key parts of his agenda such as tax cuts and the border wall.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> The Trump administration has created new protections for health workers who have religious and moral objections to certain procedures, such as abortion or assisted suicide.
TITLE=> . ARTICLE=> New indictments of 13 Russians who allegedly meddled in the 2016 election set the political world abuzz on Friday.
